<softupgrade xmlns="http://www.softaculous.com">

	<!--
		SocietyPress — Softaculous Upgrade Form

		WHY there are no fields: an upgrade replaces files and then reactivates
		the plugin so its dbDelta migrations run. Nothing about that needs the
		volunteer's input, so the form carries a single hidden field purely
		because Softaculous expects a <settings> block to exist. This mirrors the
		shipped WordPress package, which does the same thing.

		WHY nothing is excluded from being overwritten: an earlier revision
		excluded all five child themes here, on the theory that it was protecting
		customisation. It was not — a society's design lives in the database, not
		in the theme files — and the effect was that the plugin would advance to
		a new version while the child themes stayed behind. SocietyPress ships as
		one versioned set, and sp_get_theme_registry() advertises a version for
		each child theme; let the two drift apart and the Theme Gallery offers an
		update that installs and then immediately reappears, forever. wp-config.php
		and wp-content/uploads are protected by Softaculous itself.
	-->

	<settings>
		<group>
			<heading>hidden</heading>
			<input type="hidden" name="dummy" value="">
			</input>
		</group>
	</settings>

	<setuplocation>wp-admin/upgrade.php</setuplocation>

</softupgrade>
